  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Connecticut has received $19.6B in federal contract obligations so far in FY2026, with 28,551 awards at an average award size of $688K. Obligations are down 44.1% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer in the state, obligating $19.1B of the total. ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION is the largest vendor, receiving $11.6B in FY2026 to date, followed by RTX CORPORATION at $3.9B and SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION at $2.9B. Engineering Services is the largest industry by obligations at $7.1B, followed by Ship Building and Repairing at $4.6B and Aircraft Manufacturing at $3.2B. Historical obligations show variation across fiscal years, with FY21 at $18.4B, FY22 at $22.3B, FY23 at $26B, FY24 at $20B, and FY25 at $35.1B. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress. This snapshot highlights concentrated defense buying, large prime contractors tied to naval and aerospace work, and heavy spending in engineering and shipbuilding-related NAICS categories.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have federal contract obligations in Connecticut changed over recent years?",
        "body": "Obligations by fiscal year moved through $18.4B in FY21, $22.3B in FY22, $26B in FY23, $20B in FY24, $35.1B in FY25, and $19.6B in FY26 to date. Obligations are down 44.1% year over year. The FY26 total is a fiscal year to date figure, so the current-year total is partial. The multi-year pattern shows large swings driven by single-agency and prime-vendor programs."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries drive Connecticut federal contracting right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buying agency, obligating $19.1B in FY2026 to date. Engineering Services leads industries at $7.1B, Ship Building and Repairing follows at $4.6B, and Aircraft Manufacturing is next at $3.2B. Major vendors concentrate work in those sectors, with ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION at $11.6B, RTX CORPORATION at $3.9B, and SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION at $2.9B."
      }
    ]
  },
